description: TechnoRapper Mobile API auth and abuse controls must stay fail-closed
alwaysApply: true
---

# Mobile API auth

- Content GET routes require `Authorization: Bearer` only. Never accept `X-TR-App-Key` or install secrets on content routes.
- `POST /auth/register` is the only route that accepts `X-TR-App-Key`. It creates per-install credentials.
- `POST /auth/token` requires `install_id` + `install_secret` and must embed `iid` in the Bearer payload.
- Bearer validation must reject revoked/missing installs even if the HMAC token is unexpired.
- If `tr_mobile_app_key` is empty, the API must fail closed (`503`). Do not restore open-by-default access.
- Keep page/limit caps (`limit` ≤ 20, posts page ≤ 50, search page ≤ 10).
- Do not run `the_content` on API bodies; keep `wp_kses_post` (or tighter).
- Password-protected posts must not appear in list/detail/search.
- Origin rate limiting is best-effort; Cloudflare is the real DDoS control. Do not claim App Key / install keys make clone apps impossible.
